WEBVTT

00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:04.212
Cambridge English Readers, Starter Level.

00:00:04.272 --> 00:00:08.154
Why? By Philip Prowse.
 
00:00:08.214 --> 00:00:18.076
Published by Cambridge University Press.

00:00:18.136 --> 00:00:33.379
Why? By Philip Prowse.
 
00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:43.041
Chapter 1. Goodbye
 
00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:49.354
Please don't go to Glossia. says Sara.
 
00:00:49.414 --> 00:00:52.306
You're only 19.

00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:58.049
Alex is saying goodbye to Sara, his girlfriend.

00:00:58.108 --> 00:01:01.920
I must. answers Alex.
 
00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.892
I'm a soldier.

00:01:03.951 --> 00:01:05.482
It's my job.

00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:09.119
I must go where the army says.

00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:14.736
But why are you going there? asks Sara.
 
00:01:14.796 --> 00:01:19.938
We're going to stop the fighting. says Alex.
 
00:01:19.998 --> 00:01:23.328
Lots of people are dying.

00:01:23.388 --> 00:01:29.101
But why are they fighting? asks Sara.
 
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.452
I don't know. answers Alex.
 
00:01:33.512 --> 00:01:37.383
Why don't you ask? says Sara.
 
00:01:37.443 --> 00:01:40.442
You never ask questions.

00:01:40.502 --> 00:01:43.864
I know, answers Alex.

00:01:43.924 --> 00:01:48.261
I'm sorry. I hate asking questions.
 
00:01:48.321 --> 00:01:55.512
Please change, Alex, says Sara, for me.

00:01:55.572 --> 00:02:01.444
I'm going to think about you every day, says Sara.

00:02:01.504 --> 00:02:05.026
Me too, Alex answers.

00:02:05.086 --> 00:02:11.797
I can send you a text from my phone tomorrow, and I think there's email.

00:02:11.857 --> 00:02:13.728
That's good.

00:02:13.788 --> 00:02:16.829
Sara says with a little smile.

00:02:16.888 --> 00:02:19.590
I love you, Alex.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.341
And I love you too, answers Alex.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.303
Now, don't be sad.

00:02:28.363 --> 00:02:35.648
Chapter 2. We're in Glossia now
 
00:02:35.707 --> 00:02:39.879
Alex is on the plane to Glossia.

00:02:39.939 --> 00:02:43.450
He's sitting next to Sergeant Ken.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:47.772
It's Ken's second time in Glossia.

00:02:47.832 --> 00:02:52.745
Excuse me, Sergeant. Alex starts.
 
00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.476
You can call me Ken.

00:02:55.536 --> 00:02:57.658
The sergeant says.

00:02:57.718 --> 00:03:03.790
Why are they fighting in Glossia? Alex asks.
 
00:03:03.893 --> 00:03:09.567
That's not an easy question. Ken answers.
 
00:03:09.626 --> 00:03:12.818
I think it's like this.

00:03:12.878 --> 00:03:15.810
Some people have guns.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:19.932
They use the guns because they want something.

00:03:19.992 --> 00:03:24.544
Then other people get guns to fight back with.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.756
Now everyone has guns.

00:03:27.816 --> 00:03:32.667
And everyone forgets what they are fighting about.

00:03:32.727 --> 00:03:36.318
But where do the guns come from?

00:03:36.378 --> 00:03:39.130
is Alex's next question.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:44.382
People from other countries sell them to the Glossians.

00:03:44.442 --> 00:03:46.163
Ken answers.

00:03:46.223 --> 00:03:49.514
Why? asks Alex.
 
00:03:49.574 --> 00:03:55.523
Ken smiles. Money. That's why.
 
00:03:55.583 --> 00:04:00.700
Ken, can we stop people buying and selling guns?

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.591
Alex asks.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:04.951
No, we can't.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:11.152
The people who sell the guns, they're thousands of kilometres away.

00:04:11.212 --> 00:04:16.534
All we can do is help the people here in this country.

00:04:16.594 --> 00:04:18.584
answers, Ken.

00:04:18.644 --> 00:04:23.911
We're going to a famous old town called Tonek.

00:04:23.971 --> 00:04:28.609
In Tonek, lots of people are fighting each other.

00:04:28.669 --> 00:04:33.400
And some of them are also fighting us.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:39.854
There's a very loud noise, and the plane goes over to the right.

00:04:39.914 --> 00:04:43.716
What's that? shouts Alex.
 
00:04:43.776 --> 00:04:47.657
What do you think? answers Ken.
 
00:04:47.717 --> 00:04:51.088
We're in Glossia now.

00:04:51.148 --> 00:04:56.028
Is it always like this? Alex asks.
 
00:04:56.088 --> 00:04:59.089
Yes, Ken answers.

00:04:59.149 --> 00:05:05.661
But the papers say the Glossian people want us here, Alex says.

00:05:05.721 --> 00:05:08.702
The sergeant smiles.

00:05:08.762 --> 00:05:14.884
Some Glossians do, and some don't. answers, Ken.
 
00:05:14.944 --> 00:05:19.115
But we're here to help all the people.

00:05:19.175 --> 00:05:23.400
And is it always hot? asks Alex.
 
00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:29.904
Yes, laughs Ken.

00:05:29.964 --> 00:05:37.000
Chapter 3. Soldiers get out. 

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.496
Sergeant Ken and Alex drive into Tonek.

00:05:42.556 --> 00:05:45.170
People watch them.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:52.806
Alex, this is where you're living for the next six months, says Ken.

00:05:52.866 --> 00:05:58.689
Your bed's over there, and this is Hawk.

00:05:58.748 --> 00:06:05.702
A tall man with very short hair stands up and puts out his hand.

00:06:05.762 --> 00:06:08.975
Hi, he says.

00:06:09.034 --> 00:06:14.087
And that's Stefan on the bed, Ken says.

00:06:14.147 --> 00:06:17.588
Stefan smiles at Alex.

00:06:17.648 --> 00:06:19.098
Hello?

00:06:19.158 --> 00:06:22.460
Put your things down, he says.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.041
Do you want something to eat or drink?

00:06:26.101 --> 00:06:29.693
Yes please, answers Alex.

00:06:29.752 --> 00:06:33.434
I'm going now, Ken says.

00:06:33.494 --> 00:06:36.105
You must be tired Alex.

00:06:36.165 --> 00:06:39.126
Try and get some sleep tonight.

00:06:39.186 --> 00:06:42.755
We start work in the morning.

00:06:42.815 --> 00:06:45.164
Hi, Sara.

00:06:45.224 --> 00:06:48.325
It's very hot in Glossia.

00:06:48.385 --> 00:06:51.997
Sergeant Ken says we're here to help.

00:06:52.057 --> 00:06:56.429
But can we? I don't know.
 
00:06:56.489 --> 00:07:01.902
All my love, Alex.

00:07:01.962 --> 00:07:08.250
Chapter 4. First patrol. 

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:14.458
The next day, it's time for Alex's first patrol.

00:07:14.518 --> 00:07:17.509
Just do what I do.

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:19.610
Ken tells Alex.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:24.242
Stefan and Hawk are going to walk behind us.

00:07:24.302 --> 00:07:29.254
Use your eyes and ears and look everywhere.

00:07:29.314 --> 00:07:36.734
And don't forget, we never know who is a friend and who isn't.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.400
What are we looking for? asks Alex.
 
00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:47.890
Guns. answers Ken with a quick laugh
 
00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:51.913
And gunmen. Hawk says.
  
00:07:51.973 --> 00:07:54.716
He isn't laughing.

00:07:54.775 --> 00:07:58.798
But what about the people who sell the guns?

00:07:58.858 --> 00:08:00.801
Alex asks.

00:08:00.861 --> 00:08:03.072
They're not here.

00:08:03.132 --> 00:08:04.683
Hawk answers.

00:08:04.743 --> 00:08:09.354
They're far away with their money.

00:08:09.414 --> 00:08:13.775
Some people are happy to see the soldiers.

00:08:13.835 --> 00:08:16.786
They stop and say hello.

00:08:16.846 --> 00:08:21.357
But some boys aren't happy that the soldiers are there.

00:08:21.417 --> 00:08:25.818
They're throwing things at the patrol and shouting.

00:08:25.878 --> 00:08:31.056
The soldiers don't understand what the boys are shouting.

00:08:31.116 --> 00:08:34.682
Something hits Alex in the mouth.

00:08:34.742 --> 00:08:37.353
He turns with his gun.

00:08:37.413 --> 00:08:42.734
Alex isn't slow, but the boys are very fast.

00:08:42.794 --> 00:08:44.834
They run away.

00:08:44.894 --> 00:08:47.815
Alex feels his mouth.

00:08:47.875 --> 00:08:52.056
Are you okay? Stefan shouts.
 
00:08:52.116 --> 00:08:55.426
Yes, answers Alex.

00:08:55.486 --> 00:08:58.756
Then they hear a gun.

00:08:58.816 --> 00:09:02.442
Someone's shooting at them.

00:09:02.502 --> 00:09:07.910
Alex looks across the dirty street at a house.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:12.054
He sees someone at a bedroom window.

00:09:12.114 --> 00:09:17.058
Look! Up there! Alex shouts.
 
00:09:17.118 --> 00:09:22.493
Hawk turns, looks up and shoots at the window.

00:09:22.553 --> 00:09:27.281
Ken and Alex run across the street to the house.

00:09:27.341 --> 00:09:31.918
They open the front door and run up to the bedroom.

00:09:31.978 --> 00:09:36.460
Hawk and Stefan wait in the street.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:39.182
Hi, Sara.

00:09:39.242 --> 00:09:41.733
What a bad day.

00:09:41.793 --> 00:09:44.134
My first patrol.

00:09:44.195 --> 00:09:49.288
There's shooting and I see someone at a bedroom window.

00:09:49.348 --> 00:09:52.089
Hawk shoots at the window.

00:09:52.149 --> 00:09:57.520
Then Ken and I run into the house and up to the bedroom.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:00.500
But there isn't a gunmen there.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.881
It's a little boy.

00:10:02.941 --> 00:10:06.732
The boy's mother comes and shouts at us.

00:10:06.792 --> 00:10:10.066
I don't understand what she's saying, 

00:10:10.132 --> 00:10:14.006
but I can see she's very angry.

00:10:14.066 --> 00:10:19.108
I want to say sorry, but I don't speak Glossian.

00:10:19.168 --> 00:10:24.990
When we leave, the woman is shouting and the small boy is crying.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.266
I don't feel well.

00:10:27.326 --> 00:10:29.402
It's all wrong.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:32.154
What am I doing here?

00:10:32.214 --> 00:10:37.517
All my love, Alex.

00:10:37.577 --> 00:10:44.942
Chapter 5. We have no names.

00:10:45.002 --> 00:10:53.477
The next day, Sergeant Ken, Alex, Hawk and Stefan are on patrol again.

00:10:53.537 --> 00:10:55.992
It's 12 o'clock.

00:10:56.052 --> 00:11:01.038
A kilometer away, a family is finishing lunch.

00:11:01.098 --> 00:11:09.402
There's a 12-year-old boy called Happy, and an 8-year-old girl called Marina.

00:11:09.462 --> 00:11:14.614
Their mother's name is Ada, and she's very beautiful.

00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:17.176
There's no father.

00:11:17.236 --> 00:11:19.607
He's dead.

00:11:19.667 --> 00:11:26.257
In the afternoon, Ada puts away the lunch things and makes coffee.

00:11:26.317 --> 00:11:31.509
Happy is sitting on the floor in the living room with Marina.

00:11:31.569 --> 00:11:37.055
The brother and sister are laughing and playing with a doll.

00:11:37.115 --> 00:11:41.039
Ada doesn't hear the back door.

00:11:41.099 --> 00:11:43.562
Two men come in.

00:11:43.622 --> 00:11:47.386
One is tall and one is short.

00:11:47.446 --> 00:11:50.248
The short man has a bag.

00:11:50.308 --> 00:11:54.608
They're wearing white t-shirts and black trousers.

00:11:54.668 --> 00:11:57.848
And they have black masks.

00:11:57.908 --> 00:12:01.199
Ada looks at the two men.

00:12:01.259 --> 00:12:06.970
Then she shouts to her children, come here now!

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:12.211
Happy and Marina run to their mother and stand by her.

00:12:12.271 --> 00:12:16.162
They're afraid of the two men in masks.

00:12:16.222 --> 00:12:18.712
Who are you?

00:12:18.772 --> 00:12:21.504
Ada asks the men.

00:12:21.564 --> 00:12:23.996
They don't answer.

00:12:24.056 --> 00:12:30.551
The short man puts the bag down, and the tall man looks at Ada.

00:12:30.611 --> 00:12:35.985
What are your names? asks Ada.
 
00:12:36.045 --> 00:12:42.160
We have no names, and we have no faces.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:44.852
answers the tall man.

00:12:44.911 --> 00:12:47.754
We are not rich.

00:12:47.814 --> 00:12:53.062
What do you want? asks Ada.
 
00:12:53.122 --> 00:12:57.972
Nothing, answers the short man.

00:12:58.031 --> 00:13:05.388
All we want is your house for ten minutes.

00:13:05.448 --> 00:13:13.600
Chapter 6. Don’t ask stupid questions. 

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:19.540
A young woman with a baby comes in the front door.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:23.658
Who's she? asks Ada.
 
00:13:23.718 --> 00:13:27.510
Shh, says the tall man.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.800
The baby.

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:33.683
The young woman lifts up the baby.

00:13:33.743 --> 00:13:35.804
It's sleeping.

00:13:35.864 --> 00:13:40.176
Under the baby is a long gun.

00:13:40.236 --> 00:13:46.769
The tall man takes the gun and the woman puts the baby down again.

00:13:46.829 --> 00:13:52.172
What are you going to do? asks Happy.
 
00:13:52.232 --> 00:13:58.286
A soldier is going to die, answers the short man.

00:13:58.346 --> 00:14:02.248
Why? asks Happy.
 
00:14:02.308 --> 00:14:08.502
Don't ask stupid questions, says the tall man.

00:14:08.562 --> 00:14:11.664
This is our country.

00:14:11.724 --> 00:14:17.147
We don't want soldiers from other countries here.

00:14:17.207 --> 00:14:22.107
You, the short man shouts to Marina.

00:14:22.167 --> 00:14:25.366
Give me your doll.

00:14:25.426 --> 00:14:30.260
Do it! Ada tells her daughter.
 
00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:33.812
Marina gives the man her doll.

00:14:33.872 --> 00:14:39.818
He takes something out of his bag and puts it in the doll.

00:14:39.878 --> 00:14:45.652
Then he takes a phone and puts it in the doll, too.

00:14:45.712 --> 00:14:48.434
Listen, you two.

00:14:48.494 --> 00:14:51.624
The short man tells the children.

00:14:51.684 --> 00:14:55.404
You mustn't play with the doll now.

00:14:55.464 --> 00:14:57.894
Do you understand?

00:14:57.954 --> 00:15:02.066
Yes. Happy answers.
 
00:15:02.126 --> 00:15:07.900
Here, the short man says to the young woman with the baby.

00:15:07.959 --> 00:15:14.222
Take the doll and leave it in the street in front of the house.

00:15:14.282 --> 00:15:18.614
The short man speaks to the children.

00:15:18.674 --> 00:15:23.268
Go and play in front of the house now.

00:15:23.328 --> 00:15:28.942
But when you see the soldiers, you must run in again.

00:15:29.002 --> 00:15:31.484
He looks at Ada.

00:15:31.544 --> 00:15:37.929
Then you take your children out of the house by the back door.

00:15:37.989 --> 00:15:40.260
Do you understand?

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:44.014
Yes, says Ada.

00:15:44.074 --> 00:15:50.870
Happy and Marina. Go out and play in the street now.
 
00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:54.801
But don't go near the doll.

00:15:54.861 --> 00:15:59.642
The short man gives a phone to the tall man.

00:15:59.702 --> 00:16:06.815
This phone's for you, and there's a phone in the doll, he says.

00:16:06.874 --> 00:16:12.856
The tall man takes the gun and the phone up to the bedroom.

00:16:12.916 --> 00:16:16.266
The young woman goes with him.

00:16:16.326 --> 00:16:21.527
Out of the window, they can see the children in the street.

00:16:21.587 --> 00:16:24.258
And the doll.

00:16:24.318 --> 00:16:28.789
The tall man has the phone in his hand.

00:16:28.849 --> 00:16:35.421
All we can do now is wait, he tells the woman.

00:16:35.481 --> 00:16:41.042
Listen, what's that? asks the woman.
 
00:16:41.102 --> 00:16:43.740
Can you hear something?

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:47.500
Yes, the tall man answers.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.642
It's the soldiers.

00:16:49.702 --> 00:16:53.995
They're coming.

00:16:54.055 --> 00:17:01.280
Chapter 7. They're afraid of us.

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:07.363
Why are the children running away? Alex asks Hawk.
 
00:17:07.424 --> 00:17:12.303
Because they're afraid of us. Hawk answers.
 
00:17:12.363 --> 00:17:15.740
But why? asks Alex.
 
00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.890
We're here to help.

00:17:17.951 --> 00:17:21.532
Don't they know that we're their friends?

00:17:21.592 --> 00:17:26.014
The patrol gets near to Ada's house.

00:17:26.074 --> 00:17:31.045
Yes, the children must be afraid of us.

00:17:31.105 --> 00:17:33.536
Alex says to Hawk.

00:17:33.596 --> 00:17:37.741
Look, that's their doll in the street.

00:17:37.802 --> 00:17:40.327
Then they can see we’re their friends.

00:17:40.387 --> 00:17:44.218
Then they can see with their friends.

00:17:44.279 --> 00:17:48.310
Alex runs over to the doll.

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:52.372
Stop! shouts Ken.
 
00:17:52.432 --> 00:17:54.524
Alex looks up.

00:17:54.584 --> 00:17:57.575
Why? He asks.
 
00:17:57.635 --> 00:18:00.576
I'm just trying to help.

00:18:00.636 --> 00:18:04.648
Do what I say. shouts Ken.
 
00:18:04.708 --> 00:18:07.201
Come here now.

00:18:07.261 --> 00:18:13.416
Up in the bedroom, the tall man speaks to the young woman.

00:18:13.476 --> 00:18:17.660
The phone isn't working!

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:20.571
He's very angry.

00:18:20.631 --> 00:18:23.332
What about the gun?

00:18:23.392 --> 00:18:26.154
The young woman asks.

00:18:26.214 --> 00:18:34.252
The tall man looks at Hawk, then at Stefan, then Sergeant Ken.

00:18:34.312 --> 00:18:39.516
Then he looks at Alex and chooses.

00:18:39.576 --> 00:18:45.248
You're going to die, he says.

00:18:45.308 --> 00:18:48.720
The tall man shoots.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:54.092
Alex's mouth opens and he tries to say something.

00:18:54.152 --> 00:18:57.743
Then his eyes close.

00:18:57.803 --> 00:19:00.764
He doesn't say anything.

00:19:00.824 --> 00:19:03.688
He doesn't see anything.

00:19:03.748 --> 00:19:06.892
He doesn't feel anything.

00:19:06.952 --> 00:19:09.663
He's dead.

00:19:09.723 --> 00:19:13.485
Hawk turns and looks up.

00:19:13.545 --> 00:19:18.097
He sees someone at the bedroom window.

00:19:18.158 --> 00:19:20.378
Up there!

00:19:20.438 --> 00:19:23.940
Hawk shouts and shoots.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:29.816
Then Ken and Stefan shoot at the window.

00:19:29.876 --> 00:19:36.050
The young woman helps the tall man down to the living room.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:42.702
Here! Quick! Take the gun!
 
00:19:42.762 --> 00:19:45.742
He says to the young woman.

00:19:45.802 --> 00:19:51.174
She takes the gun and puts it under the baby.

00:19:51.234 --> 00:19:52.625
Come on!

00:19:52.685 --> 00:19:54.856
The soldiers are coming!

00:19:54.916 --> 00:19:56.886
shouts the short man.

00:19:56.946 --> 00:20:00.250
You must see a doctor!

00:20:00.310 --> 00:20:04.455
I can't go anywhere!

00:20:04.515 --> 00:20:06.626
the tall man says.

00:20:06.686 --> 00:20:11.229
You two go! Now!
 
00:20:11.289 --> 00:20:14.580
He closes his eyes.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:23.572
Chapter 8. Don't say anything.
 
00:20:23.632 --> 00:20:31.750
The young woman and the short man run out of the back of the house.

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:36.291
Ada and the children are waiting there.

00:20:36.352 --> 00:20:41.282
Where's your friend? Ada asks.
 
00:20:41.342 --> 00:20:45.614
Dead. The young woman answers.
 
00:20:45.674 --> 00:20:49.445
Why? asks Happy.
 
00:20:49.505 --> 00:20:52.776
Because of the soldiers.

00:20:52.836 --> 00:20:55.326
The young woman says.

00:20:55.386 --> 00:21:00.640
She turns and walks away fast with the baby.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:05.832
I hate soldiers. Happy says.
 
00:21:05.892 --> 00:21:09.605
Don't tell the soldiers about us.

00:21:09.665 --> 00:21:12.416
The short man tells Ada.

00:21:12.476 --> 00:21:18.370
He takes off his mask and she can see his face now.

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:21.936
And your boy's coming with me.

00:21:21.996 --> 00:21:27.978
Don't say anything to the soldiers, or he dies!

00:21:28.038 --> 00:21:32.624
He takes Happy's hand and starts to run off.

00:21:32.684 --> 00:21:35.778
No! shouts Ada.
 
00:21:35.838 --> 00:21:39.541
Don't take him! Happy!
 
00:21:39.601 --> 00:21:45.634
Ken, Hawk and Stefan run in the front door of the house.

00:21:45.694 --> 00:21:49.226
They see the dead man in the living room.

00:21:49.287 --> 00:21:52.428
Stefan runs up to the bedroom.

00:21:52.488 --> 00:21:56.792
Hawk and Ken go out to the back of the house.

00:21:56.852 --> 00:22:00.834
They find Ada and Marina there.

00:22:00.894 --> 00:22:04.923
Hawk speaks a little Glossian.

00:22:04.983 --> 00:22:09.121
Where are they? He shouts.
 
00:22:09.181 --> 00:22:11.992
Ada says nothing.

00:22:12.052 --> 00:22:16.506
Then, Hawk sees two people running away.

00:22:16.566 --> 00:22:19.417
A man and a boy.

00:22:19.477 --> 00:22:21.778
Hawk doesn't wait.

00:22:21.838 --> 00:22:23.830
He shoots.

00:22:23.890 --> 00:22:28.612
No! Ada shouts.
 
00:22:28.672 --> 00:22:34.315
Ken takes Ada and Marina into the house.

00:22:34.375 --> 00:22:42.698
Half an hour later, two kilometers away, the young woman is walking with the baby.

00:22:42.759 --> 00:22:47.802
Two soldiers see her and ask her to stop.

00:22:47.862 --> 00:22:50.243
Where are you going?

00:22:50.303 --> 00:22:52.994
asks one of the soldiers.

00:22:53.054 --> 00:22:57.166
To the shops, answers the woman.

00:22:57.226 --> 00:23:00.628
I'm going to buy some food.

00:23:00.688 --> 00:23:03.695
She smiles at the soldiers.

00:23:03.755 --> 00:23:05.672
What's in there?

00:23:05.732 --> 00:23:07.964
The soldier shouts.

00:23:08.024 --> 00:23:10.236
My baby.

00:23:10.297 --> 00:23:14.531
The woman says, please don't shout.

00:23:14.591 --> 00:23:16.804
He's sleeping.

00:23:16.864 --> 00:23:19.666
She smiles again.

00:23:19.726 --> 00:23:22.760
Okay, you can go.

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:29.614
Says one of the soldiers and smiles at her.

00:23:29.674 --> 00:23:36.657
Chapter 9. Why?
 
00:23:36.717 --> 00:23:41.680
There are lots of soldiers at Ada's house now.

00:23:41.740 --> 00:23:46.952
They take Alex and the tall man away in a car.

00:23:47.012 --> 00:23:51.354
A Glossian man is helping Sergeant Ken.

00:23:51.414 --> 00:23:55.126
He's asking Ada lots of questions.

00:23:55.186 --> 00:23:58.608
But Ada doesn't answer.

00:23:58.668 --> 00:24:02.274
All she can think of is happy.

00:24:02.334 --> 00:24:04.358
Where is he?

00:24:04.418 --> 00:24:06.650
Is he dead?

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:14.894
She takes Marina's hand and listens to the questions, but she doesn't answer.

00:24:14.954 --> 00:24:20.187
The soldiers leave Ada and Marina in the house.

00:24:20.247 --> 00:24:25.029
That evening, Ada hears a noise at the back door.

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:26.920
It's dark.

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:31.845
She opens the door and sees Happy there.

00:24:31.905 --> 00:24:37.100
Are the soldiers here? asks Happy.
 
00:24:37.160 --> 00:24:47.204
No. Ada says with a big smile and takes Happy in her arms.
 
00:24:47.264 --> 00:24:53.908
Alex, why don't you answer my emails?

00:24:53.968 --> 00:24:56.248
Are you okay?

00:24:56.308 --> 00:24:58.559
Why don't you write?

00:24:58.620 --> 00:25:01.579
Why? Why?
 
00:25:01.639 --> 00:25:25.000
All my love, Sara.